sh":"fcf4fac7abfefe5462a13c3f59b791cc089049d97efc0cfaf0b51fe2dabdb655","event_uuid":"21f0af71-77f4-459e-9f2e-fbb4e4a9371b","position":{"commit_sha":"746c5ba0e1324b4bb30fa88dde0f46bc41fc546a","position":"1788109615491051596-21f0af71-77f4-459e-9f2e-fbb4e4a9371b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"52e4e9b46151969fa10ff3c72a6c233392b469304de14166896d8668e7a65326","event_uuid":"212f162b-f5d0-43e5-b83f-f42019090e49","position":{"commit_sha":"07f9141bad8e9ef0b4437d791d76bf8159cf03c6","position":"1788111251273944846-212f162b-f5d0-43e5-b83f-f42019090e49"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788029145159590662,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"c06b763d-6893-4c66-b07b-7808df5c6b45","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"5d19-52e0-7c26-47fb"},{"link_uuid":"5622bbb6-0599-4dca-a150-f773a9a7a9a7","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"4c80-edd3-20f1-4dff"},{"link_uuid":"17c5467e-1eea-429c-b9fc-c64aab31bee3","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"efd4-847d-f7ad-47bc"},{"link_uuid":"a5359bfb-d07e-4170-8689-1bcd0031c361","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"cdc1-5a12-4676-49a7"},{"link_uuid":"ce9aed6b-c99a-45c0-b6b7-cbd6d5b031cc","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"a144-5838-3265-405e"},{"link_uuid":"b79d4e15-f29e-40f7-ab03-dbb7d33982c9","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"abe4-a071-2d0f-4453"},{"link_uuid":"21f0af71-77f4-459e-9f2e-fbb4e4a9371b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"85a9-fa7b-f39e-4f44"},{"link_uuid":"212f162b-f5d0-43e5-b83f-f42019090e49","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"491a-857f-df77-4db5"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nPass 2 (`src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/verify.py`, questions in `verify_models.py`, prompts `reviewers/plan_review_verifier*.md`, `temperature: 0`, standard class = Sonnet on Bedrock) is the cheapest LLM pass. A question/prompt change can be measured by re-verifying the *stored* Pass-1 findings and comparing to the stored answers.\n\n**Production input, byte-identical — exact seam call.** `verify.finding_listing(batch)` (verify.py:101-108) renders ONLY `claim`/`criteria`/`evidence`/`impact` per finding — NOT `location`. The real signature (verify.py:345) is `verify_findings(findings, *, context, run_chunk, window_tokens, est_tokens, headroom=DEFAULT_VERIFY_WINDOW_HEADROOM)`. Production's plan-review wrapper (`sizing.verify_request_chunks`, sizing.py:187-206) supplies `window_tokens=sizing.largest_window_tokens(model)` and `est_tokens=det_floor.est_tokens` (`from rebar.llm.plan_review import det_floor, sizing`). The replay calls `verify_findings(stored_findings, context=plan_context, run_chunk=<candidate runner>, window_tokens=sizing.largest_window_tokens(standard_class_model), est_tokens=det_floor.est_tokens)`.\n\n**Missing-answer handling.** `verify_findings` returns `{index: {severity_attributes, binary}}` plus `\"omitted\": [index, ...]`; a chunk whose `run_chunk` raises contributes NO verifications (absent from the result dict). Excluded from κ/agreement with a reported \"no-answer\" count per question.\n\n**Ledger — flat per-sample, not token-derived.** `ledger.estimate(tier, sample_n)` returns `PER_SAMPLE_ESTIMATE_USD[tier] * sample_n` — a FIXED historical constant. Pre-flight is `ledger.reserve(ledger.estimate(\"tier1\", n))`, exactly as tier0/labels/parity already do.\n\n**Tier1's candidate is a NEW concept, not Pass-3's `Candidate`/`CANDIDATES`.** Tier1 introduces its own `VerifierCandidate` in a NEW `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/verifier_candidates.py`: `@dataclass(frozen=True) class VerifierCandidate: prompt_path: str | None = None` (`None` = production's shipped prompt/questions) plus `load_verifier_candidate(path_or_none) -> VerifierCandidate`.\n\n**Distribution shift, defined — categorical vs continuous axes.** `decide.validity(binary)` (decide.py:67-74) returns a CONTINUOUS `round(mean(graded scores), 4) ∈ [0,1]`; `priority = round(validity * impact, 4)` (decide.py:681) is likewise a continuous derived scalar — NEITHER has a categorical vocabulary the verifier emits. Only the severity-attribute/binary answers (impact's inputs) are categorical (`verify_models.py`'s closed Literal sets). Distribution shift is therefore computed uniformly over FIXED bins for every axis: impact's underlying categorical severity-attribute/binary answers use their own closed vocabulary directly as \"bins\"; validity and priority are binned into 10 FIXED, equal-width `[0.0,0.1), [0.1,0.2), ..., [0.9,1.0]` buckets. For every axis: per-bucket COUNT DELTA (stored vs candidate) plus TOTAL VARIATION DISTANCE between the two bucketed distributions, computed per stratum and overall.\n\n## Approach\n\nBuild `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/tier1.py`, `sampling.py`, `verifier_candidates.py`:\n\n- Sample selection: deterministic stratified sample (strata: verdict, leaf/container, finding-count bucket, project overlay/store, `impact_model_version`), size N, seed fixed; only `verified` rows; only rows whose `provider_provenance.ran_model` is the current standard-class model.\n- Pre-flight: `ledger.reserve(ledger.estimate(\"tier1\", n))` before any call.\n- For each sampled review: `verify_findings(stored_findings, context=plan_context, run_chunk=<candidate's PydanticAIRunner pinned to standard-class Bedrock>, window_tokens=sizing.largest_window_tokens(model), est_tokens=det_floor.est_tokens)`. Collect the result dict + `omitted`.\n- Compare to stored answers per question: κ + raw agreement, EXCLUDING (with a reported count) any finding absent from the candidate result or in `omitted`; per-attribute agreement for severity attributes; distribution shift (per-axis bucketing above) for validity/impact/priority; hand both answer sets to Tier-0 for downstream verdict/label metrics.\n- Reproduction run (`VerifierCandidate(prompt_path=None)`) is the commissioning run: its agreement is the Pass-2 noise floor at temperature 0, stored with the labels.\n- Record the model id per result; reject a result whose model id isn't the standard class at diff time.\n\n`src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/__main__.py`: add a `tier1` subparser (`--candidate <path-or-omitted-for-current>`, `--n`, `--seed`, plus the shared `--store`/`--cache-dir`/`--out-dir`) and an `args.command == \"tier1\"` dispatch branch, mirroring `tier0`'s structure.\n\n`src/rebar/llm/evals/eval_solver.py`: add the verifier `run_case` arm.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/tier1.py`, `sampling.py`, `verifier_candidates.py` (new)\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/__main__.py` (edited — `tier1` subparser + dispatch)\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/eval_solver.py` (verifier `run_case` arm)\n- `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/replay/tier1-*.md` (generated)\n- `tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_tier1.py` (new)\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit: sampling is deterministic for a seed and respects strata; a `FakeRunner` returning canned verifications yields the expected per-question agreement table with the correct κ/raw-agreement numbers on a known fixture; a finding present in stored but absent/omitted from candidate results is excluded from agreement and counted; distribution shift for validity/priority correctly buckets a known set of continuous values into the 10 fixed bins and computes count-delta/TVD; a run whose `ledger.estimate(\"tier1\", n)` exceeds the ledger allocation is refused before any call; a result with a non-standard-class model id is rejected at diff time; `VerifierCandidate(prompt_path=None)` reproduces the production `finding_listing`/`verify_request_chunks` input byte-for-byte (regression test comparing against `sizing.verify_request_chunks`'s own chunking on the same fixture); `__main__.py`'s `tier1` subcommand dispatches correctly. Live (commissioning, ≤$40): the reproduction run on N=60.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `python -m rebar.llm.evals.plan_replay tier1 --candidate <path> --n N` produces per-question agreement (with no-answer counts), distribution shift, and downstream Tier-0 metrics for a stratified sample; checked by one generated report.\n- [ ] The reproduction run (`VerifierCandidate(prompt_path=None)`) is recorded with its per-question agreement as the Pass-2 noise floor; checked by the report and the labels file.\n- [ ] Every call in the run is priced via `ledger.estimate(\"tier1\", n)`/`ledger.reserve` and uses the Bedrock standard-class model id; checked by the ledger rows for the run.\n- [ ] Commissioning spend for this ticket ≤ $40; checked by the ledger.\n- [ ] Unit tests pass in `make test`.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/tier1.py","reason":"Pass-2 replay"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/sampling.py","reason":"stratified sampler"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/evals/eval_solver.py","reason":"verifier run_case arm"},{"path":"docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/replay/","reason":"generated reports"},{"path":"tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_tier1.py","reason":"unit tests"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/verifier_candidates.py","reason":"new VerifierCandidate concept, distinct from Pass-3 Candidate registry"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/__main__.py","reason":"tier1 subparser + dispatch"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_subcall_class_selection.py","reason":"register the two new RunRequest sites in the model-provenance ratchet"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["depends_on","4c80-edd3-20f1-4dff"],["depends_on","5d19-52e0-7c26-47fb"],["depends_on","efd4-847d-f7ad-47bc"],["parent","759e-7dc1-675c-4877"],["relates_to","491a-857f-df77-4db5"],["relates_to","85a9-fa7b-f39e-4f44"],["relates_to","a144-5838-3265-405e"],["relates_to","abe4-a071-2d0f-4453"],["relates_to","cdc1-5a12-4676-49a7"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"759e-7dc1-675c-4877","parent_status_uuid":"c2ab2f2b-5263-4292-b510-0d18aa6b5125","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["plan-review","evals","tier-1","pass-2"],"ticket_id":"53ab-bdf6-de1c-4bb1","ticket_type":"story","title":"Tier-1 harness: replay Pass-2 impact/validity questions on stored Pass-1 findings (Sonnet via Bedrock, budgeted)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f563db18-ef1d-442f-aa94-08bb34d16525","3d739770-4989-4eba-8b27-99455c53d38a","d08cdf9a-901c-4dee-b6d4-1eaff672b822","7ed47365-f4c0-4106-9d28-02d9b86df9d6","c2ab2f2b-5263-4292-b510-0d18aa6b5125","6bd98289-6d1c-404d-84c9-ac97408f4a08","9ad9017f-ce2c-40d4-9006-64b542989b0d","a5359bfb-d07e-4170-8689-1bcd0031c361","ce9aed6b-c99a-45c0-b6b7-cbd6d5b031cc","b79d4e15-f29e-40f7-ab03-dbb7d33982c9","21f0af71-77f4-459e-9f2e-fbb4e4a9371b","212f162b-f5d0-43e5-b83f-f42019090e49"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788113686839132312,"uuid":"9b360f8e-2f53-4d60-9127-007f24965029"}